<title>SWITZERLAND: Japan approves Ciba gene altered corn.</title>
<headline>Japan approves Ciba gene altered corn.</headline>
<dateline>BASLE, Switzerland 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ciba-Geigy AG said Japanese health authorities have determined that Ciba's genetically altered corn meets Japan's safety requirements for food and food additives and approved the corn for human consumption.</p>
<p>Ciba said the corn product contains a gene which enables the plant to protect itself against the European corn borer.</p>
<p>In approving the product, Japanese authorities concur with the judgement of their colleagues in the U.S., Canada and France, Ciba also said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
